From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 22:24:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06936/11362] [outer-loop] exp5586: full-roster leaderboard
 check confirms auto_hud_mask levels_gained win

The "next check" on the deferred levels_gained question (REQ-ARC-WMTE-5583).
Used the project's own standing pre-submission measurement tool
(scripts/arc_leaderboard_eval.py) at full scale -- all 11 CLAIMED games (a
materially larger, entirely disjoint roster from exp5584's 6 or exp5585's
3), budget=2500 -- rather than another narrow bespoke A/B. This bare
"explorer" config runs at ~0.02s/action (vs exp5584/exp5585's
1.75-11.5s/action), so the larger roster/budget that finally had headroom
was affordable in ~97s wall-clock for both arms combined, no background run
needed.

Result: auto_hud_mask=False reaches 1 total level (only lp85);
auto_hud_mask=True reaches 5 total levels (lp85, cd82, sp80, su15, tu93).
adversarial_verify.py returns zero flags. The experiment's own adversarial
check (mask_fired_matches_gain_pattern) confirms every per-game delta is on
a HUD-positive game and zero deltas on any HUD-negative game -- ruling out
an unrelated confound. This is a real, clean, non-confounded levels_gained
win, closing the deferred question for the offline-measurable portion
sooner than expected (via a broader/cheaper harness, not live-submission
telemetry, though that remains the standing authority for true hidden-eval
numbers). Updated REQ-ARC-WMTE-5583 with a follow-up resolution note.

